323,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.5425,"shared":21,"play_caller":"Mike LaFleur"}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"CAR","distance":0.5541,"shared":22,"play_caller":"Ejiro Evero"},{"season":2022,"team":"GB","distance":0.6236,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYG","distance":0.6511,"shared":22,"play_caller":null},{"season":2019,"team":"ARI","distance":0.6761,"shared":18,"play_caller":"Vance Joseph"},{"season":2024,"team":"PIT","distance":0.6848,"shared":22,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Buccaneers went 9-8 in 2023 and outscored opponents 348 to 325. The offense ranked 14th in EPA per play and the defense 18th in EPA allowed, so neither side stood out much. Their most distinctive traits were the fewest backs in the backfield and the 2nd highest Cover 3 rate in the league.","offense":"The Buccaneers offense was a little above average by EPA per play, and it was much better passing the ball than running it. Their run and pass mix stayed close to what game situations called for. Their biggest outliers in how they lined up were the fewest backs in the backfield in the league. Baker Mayfield ran the passing game, with Mike Evans leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Buccaneers defense was about average by EPA allowed per play. It was much better against the run than the pass, ranking 4th and 23rd. Vita Vea was as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise was YaYa Diaby, who had 7.5 sacks while playing only 46% of the snaps, after not being a regular on this defense last season. Schematically, they had the 2nd highest Cover 3 rate in the league.","special":"The Buccaneers were about average in how often they went for it on fourth down. Their kickers made 94% of field goals, which was well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 17% of the money on the books.","players":"Baker Mayfield played nearly every snap at quarterback and threw for 4,044 yards. Mike Evans was the clear top target with 25% of the looks and 1,255 receiving yards. Rachaad White handled most of the work in the backfield with 72% of the carries. On defense, YaYa Diaby led the team with 7.5 sacks and Antoine Winfield Jr. picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Dave Canales called the offense and Todd Bowles called the defense. Their offense looked most like the 2025 Raiders under Chip Kelly and the 2025 Colts under Shane Steichen. Their defense looked most like the 2023 Panthers under Ejiro Evero and the 2022 Packers.","trends":"The offense went from 22nd in EPA per play in 2022 to 14th in 2023, a big step forward. The defense moved from 12th in EPA allowed per play in 2022 to 18th in 2023, a modest decline. The biggest change in approach was play-action rate, which went from 13% to 22%.","notes":"Every data source is available for 2023. This season uses the newer formation labels, which group singleback, I formation and empty sets together as under center, so those older formation rates are not shown."}}